G1106.def:
γνώμη, -ης, ἡ 
(γιγνώσκω), [in LXX: Da TH 2:15 (דָּת), Ps 82(83):3 (סוֹד), elsewhere, chiefly II Es, for טְעֵם ;] 
__1. a means of knowing, a token (Theogn.). 
__2. In Attic writers, the mind, its operations and results (see Edwards, Lex., App., A); 
__(a) mind, understanding; 
__(b) purpose, intention: Actes 20:3; 
__(with) judgment, opinion: 1 Corinthiens 1:10, Apocalypse 17:13; 
__(d) counsel, advice: 1 Corinthiens 7:25, 40 2 Corinthiens 8:10, Phm 14; 
__(e) royal purpose, decree (as in Da, I and II Es): Apocalypse 17:17 (Cremer, 671).
†

G1121.def:
γράμμα, -τος, τό 
(γράφω), [in LXX for סֵפֶר, etc. ;] 
__1. that which is traced or drawn, a picture. 
__2. that which is written; 
__(1) a character, letter: Galates 6:11; 
__(2) a writing, a written document; 
__(a) a bill or account: Luc 16:6, 7; 
__(b) a letter: Actes 28:21; 
__(with) τὰ ἱερὰ γ., the sacred writings, i.e. the OT: 2 Timothée 3:15 (so in Philo, Vit. Mos., iii, 39) ; 
__(d) τὸ γ., the letter, the written word as an external authority in contrast with the direct influence of the Spirit as manifested in the new Covenant: Romains 2:27, 29 7:6, 2 Corinthiens 3:6, 7; 
__(3) τὰ γ., letters, i.e. learning: Jean 7:15, Actes 26:24. (In π. an illiterate person is very frequently referred to as γράμματα μ᾽̀ εἰδότης, and this "never means anything else than inability to write": MM, Exp., x; but see also Cremer, 166; DCG, i, 202; ii, 584.)
†

G1125.def:
γράφω, [in LXX chiefly for כּתב ]; 
__1. to scrape, graze (Hom.), and later (Hdt.) to sketch, draw. 
__2. to write; 
__(a) of forming or tracing letters on writing material: Jhn.8:[6], Galates 6:11, 2 Thessaloniciens 3:17; 
__(b) to express in writing, commit to writing, record: Luc 1:63, Jean 19:21, 22 Apocalypse 1:11, 19 al.; of scripture as a standing authority (Deiss., BS, 112ff.), γέγραπται, it stands written (Luther), Matthieu 4:4, Marc 7:6, Luc 4:8, Romains 1:17, 1 Corinthiens 1:31, al.; id. before ἐν, Marc 1:2, Actes 1:20, al.; with accusative, to write of: Jean 1:46, Romains 10:5; before περί, Matthieu 26:24, Marc 14:21, Jean 5:46; al.; with dative (WM, §31, 4), Luc 18:31; id. before ἵνα (M, Pr., 207f.), Marc 12:19, Luc 20:28; κατὰ τ. γεγραμμένον, 2 Corinthiens 4:13; γεγραμμένον ἐστί, Jean 2:17; ἐγράφη, Romains 4:24; ἐπ᾽ αὐτῷ γεγραμμένα, Jean 12:16; 
__(with) of writing directions or information, with dative of person(s): Romains 15:15, 2 Corinthiens 7:12, al.; 
__(d) of that which contains the record or message: βιβλίον, Marc 10:4, Jean 21:25, Apocalypse 5:1; τίτλον, Jean 19:19; ἐπιστολήν, Actes 23:25; ἐντολήν, Marc 10:5 (cf. ἀπο-, ἐγ-, ἐπι-, κατα-, προ-).

G1140.def:
δαιμόνιον, -ου, τό
(neut. of δαιμόνιος, -α, -ον, divine), [in LXX (so also in π; see MM, Exp., x) for שֵׁד, אֱלִיל, (frequently in To) ;] 
__1. as in cl.; 
__(a) the Divine power, Deity (Hdt., Plat., al.); 
__(b) an inferior divinity, deity or demon (as in magical π, Deiss., BS, 281; MM, Exp., x): ξένα δ., Actes 17:18. 
__2. (a) in OT, heathen deities, false gods (e.g. Deutéronome 32:17, Psa.95 (96):5); 
__(b) in NT, evil spirits, demons: θύουσιν δαιμονίοις, 1 Corinthiens 10:20; διδασκαλίαι δαιμονίων, 1 Timothée 4:1; προσκυνεῖν τὰ δ., Apocalypse 9:20; ἄρχων τῶν δ., Matthieu 9:34; especially (syn. with πνεῦμα ἀκάθαρτον) as operating upon and "possessing" (of. δαιμονίζομαι) men: Matthieu 11:18, and al.; εἰσέρχεσθαι δ. εἰς. . ., Luc 8:30; δ. ἔχειν, Luc 4:33; δ. ἐκβάλλειν, Matthieu 7:22 In the phrase πνεῦμα δαιμονίου ἀκαθάρτου, Luc 4:33, the wider cl. usage (1. b) is recognised, ἀκ. being elsewhere in NT, the epithet of πν., and δ. = πν. ἀκ. (see ICC, in l; Cremer, 168)

G1166.def:
δείκνυμι, δεικνύω (see Bl., § 23, 1; Veitch, see word), 
[in LXX chiefly for רָאָה hi. ;] 
to show, with accusative of thing(s) (of person(s)), dative of person(s); 
__(a) to show, exhibit: Matthieu 4:8 8:4, Marc 1:44 14:15, Luc 4:5 5:14 20:24 22:12 24:40, Jean 2:18 5:20 10:32; 20:20 Actes 7:3" (LXX), 1 Timothée 6:15, Apocalypse 17:1 21:9, 10 22:1, 8, pass., Hébreux 8:5 (LXX); 
__(b) to make known: Matthieu 16:21, Jean 14:8, 9, Actes 10:28, 1 Corinthiens 12:31, Apocalypse 1:1 4:1 22:6; 
__(with) to prove: Jacques 2:18 3:13.†

G1175.def:
δεισιδαιμονία, -ας, ἡ 
(δεισιδαίμων, which see); 
__1. fear of the gods; 
__(a) piety, religion; 
__(b) superstition. 
__2. Objectively, a religion: Actes 25:19 (Cremer, 72, 682).†

G1189.def:
δέομαι 
(mid. of δέω, II, which see, as depon.) [in LXX for חנן, etc. ;] 
to want for oneself; 
__1. to want, need: 
__(a) absol.; 
__(b) with genitive 
__2. to beg, request, beseech, pray; 
__(i) in general: absol., Actes 26:3, WH; with genitive of person(s), Luc 5:12; 8:28; 38 (ἐδεῖτο; T, ἐδέετο, cf. Veitch, see word δέω) 9:38, Actes 8:34; 21:39, 2 Corinthiens 5:20, Galates 4:12; before ἵνα, Luc 9:40; before τό, with inf., 2 Corinthiens 10:2; with genitive of person(s) and of thing(s), 2 Corinthiens 8:4; 
__(ii) of prayer to God: absol., Actes 4:31; before εἴ πως, Romains 1:10; ἵνα, Luc 21:36; 22:32; εἰς τό, 1 Thessaloniciens 3:10; ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ πρὸς τ. κύριον, ὅπως, Actes 8:24; with genitive, τοῦ κυρίου, ὅπως, Matthieu 9:38, Luc 10:2; τοῦ Θεοῦ, Actes 10:2; before εἰ ἄρα, Actes 8:22.† 
SYN.: αἰτέω, and cf. δέησις.
